  "description": "Phonetic name encoding and sound-alike matching for .NET: Soundex, Refined Soundex, Metaphone, Double Metaphone (primary and alternate codes), NYSIIS, Match Rating Approach (encoder and comparison), Caverphone 1.0 and 2.0, and Cologne Phonetic (Koelner Phonetik). Encode names by sound so that Robert and Rupert, Catherine and Kathryn, Smith and Smyth match. Every algorithm is a faithful port of a named reference (Apache commons-codec), cross-checked against jellyfish, with a one-line SoundsLike matcher and per-algorithm comparison semantics. The maintained successor to the dead Phonix. Zero external dependencies.",
